# Testing and Verification

This rule does not authorize Memnara implementation.

## Verify before relying

- Verify APIs, package names, and versions before depending on them.
- Verify emulator functionality against the selected emulator after one is formally chosen.
- Verify RAM addresses and structures against the actual target game and ROM version.
- Never invent RAM mappings. Never invent package names or emulator capabilities.

## Honesty labels

Clearly distinguish **verified**, **mocked**, **inferred**, and **unverified** behavior.

- Never fabricate test results.
- Never report mocked behavior as live integration.
- Never mark a milestone complete without demonstrated acceptance criteria.

## Tests

- Cover critical logic: config, parsers, actions, state machines, memory, control ownership, and save/reload.
- Add regression tests after meaningful bug fixes when appropriate.
- Prefer recorded fixtures so every test does not require live model inference.
